  "limits": [
    "C8 assumes concurrent EP ranks and serial layer barriers. Grant the largest receiver at every layer, full exposure and zero replacement cost. The graph uses each actual rank/epoch and charges every scheduled start before the endpoint. A different critical receiver, cross-phase overlap or launch finishing after deadline reduces the credit.",
    "Dense-copy rate and one effective read of each intermediate are calibrated assumptions, not hardware ceilings. Cache hits, inter-core forwarding, and repeated GMM2 tile reads determine real net traffic. Other readers still need the activation. The read-equivalent threshold counts extra eliminated off-chip reads NET of replacement deliveries.",
    "Ordinary request counters lack receiver-level counts. Project the highest of the four observed eager peak concentration ratios onto the request’s own prompt. Other requests sharing a wave are excluded from its prompt. Charge each observed graph using the largest frozen graph sample. Timing denominators from both stock generations remain separate from that projection.",
    "Native stage fractions are medians across instrumented Vector cores including flags, with concurrent Cube and EP work. They are neither exclusive activation time nor request savings. Credit from barriers, changing ownership or expert placement is outside this estimate.",
    "Different dtypes, group quantization policies and draft experts have separate row and scale contracts. This screen does not transfer to them."
  ],
